    "dur": 8.04
  },
  "In a longer line, powers are done first, before times. Three squared is nine, and two times nine is eighteen.": {
    "file": "in-a-longer-line-powers-are-done-first-b-461bf4.mp3",
    "dur": 7.82
  },
  "Make three squared. Put on threes.": {
    "file": "make-three-squared-put-on-threes-31f860.mp3",
    "dur": 2.4
  },
  "Ten squared equals one hundred.": {
    "file": "ten-squared-equals-one-hundred-a77548.mp3",
    "dur": 1.78
  },
  "Sixteen beads make a square.": {
    "file": "sixteen-beads-make-a-square-18893e.mp3",
    "dur": 1.73
  },
  "Which number, squared, makes sixteen?": {
    "file": "which-number-squared-makes-sixteen-b647b3.mp3",
    "dur": 2.16
  },
  "Sixteen beads, in two rows. Can they make a square?": {
    "file": "sixteen-beads-in-two-rows-can-they-make--14ca7a.mp3",
    "dur": 3.55
  },
  "Yes. Four rows of four.": {
    "file": "yes-four-rows-of-four-4ff5c4.mp3",
    "dur": 1.39
  },
  "Four squared equals sixteen.": {
    "file": "four-squared-equals-sixteen-39c0e1.mp3",
    "dur": 1.51
  },
  "Now go the other way: from sixteen, back to the side of its square. We need a sign for that.": {
    "file": "now-go-the-other-way-from-sixteen-back-t-e7f276.mp3",
    "dur": 6.12
  },
  "This is the square root sign.": {
    "file": "this-is-the-square-root-sign-b532a1.mp3",
    "dur": 1.42
  },
  "The square root of sixteen equals four.": {
    "file": "the-square-root-of-sixteen-equals-four-15e368.mp3",
    "dur": 2.09
  },
  "It asks: which number, squared, makes sixteen? Four. That is the side of the square.": {
    "file": "it-asks-which-number-squared-makes-sixte-a919d1.mp3",
    "dur": 6.05
  },
  "Squaring takes four to sixteen. The square root brings sixteen back to four.": {
    "file": "squaring-takes-four-to-sixteen-the-squar-f87ba7.mp3",
    "dur": 4.46
  },
  "The square root of nine is three. Of twenty-five, five. Of one hundred, ten.": {
    "file": "the-square-root-of-nine-is-three-of-twen-458062.mp3",
    "dur": 5.21
  },
  "The line on top shows how far the root reaches. Here it covers nine plus sixteen. That is twenty-five, and its root is five.": {
    "file": "the-line-on-top-shows-how-far-the-root-r-796a67.mp3",
    "dur": 9.1
  },
  "Here each root has a short line of its own. Three plus four is seven. The line groups what is under it, as brackets do.": {
    "file": "here-each-root-has-a-short-line-of-its-o-20b73f.mp3",
    "dur": 8.02
  },
  "Ten beads cannot make a square: three rows of three leave one over. So the square root of ten is more than three, and less than four.": {
    "file": "ten-beads-cannot-make-a-square-three-row-e0707b.mp3",
    "dur": 8.98
  },
  "Nine beads make this square. Build one side of it.": {
    "file": "nine-beads-make-this-square-build-one-si-a1ff32.mp3",
    "dur": 2.69
  },
  "The square root of one hundred equals ten.": {
    "file": "the-square-root-of-one-hundred-equals-te-120246.mp3",
    "dur": 2.21
  },
  "The square root of ten is between three and four.": {
    "file": "the-square-root-of-ten-is-between-three--4c135f.mp3",
    "dur": 3.05
  },
  "How do we write a number that is between three and four?": {
    "file": "how-do-we-write-a-number-that-is-between-ae7b5d.mp3",
    "dur": 2.76
  },
  "Two whole beads, and three slices of a bead cut into ten. Is that nearer to two, or nearer to three?": {
    "file": "two-whole-beads-and-three-slices-of-a-be-5cf8d3.mp3",
    "dur": 8.33
  },
  "Nearer to two. Three slices are less than half a bead.": {
    "file": "nearer-to-two-three-slices-are-less-than-6da0ae.mp3",
    "dur": 3.53
  },
  "Two, and three tenths.": {
    "file": "two-and-three-tenths-dc500d.mp3",
    "dur": 1.37
  },
  "We need a short way to write whole ones and parts in one number.": {
    "file": "we-need-a-short-way-to-write-whole-ones--f893d0.mp3",
    "dur": 2.95
  },
  "This dot is the decimal point.": {
    "file": "this-dot-is-the-decimal-point-5e5a6f.mp3",
    "dur": 1.7
  },
  "We read it: two point three.": {
    "file": "we-read-it-two-point-three-82a040.mp3",
    "dur": 1.8
  },
  "The point shows where the whole ones end. Next to it, on the right, come the tenths.": {
    "file": "the-point-shows-where-the-whole-ones-end-a671bb.mp3",
    "dur": 5.33
  },
  "Cut one slice into ten, and you have hundredths. They come next: two point three five.": {
    "file": "cut-one-slice-into-ten-and-you-have-hund-69a485.mp3",
    "dur": 5.76
  },
  "Five tenths is a half. So zero point five equals one half.": {
    "file": "five-tenths-is-a-half-so-zero-point-five-5240a9.mp3",
    "dur": 3.34
  },
  "This is the percent sign.": {
    "file": "this-is-the-percent-sign-c02839.mp3",
    "dur": 1.42
  },
  "Percent means out of a hundred. Twenty-five percent is twenty-five out of a hundred.": {
    "file": "percent-means-out-of-a-hundred-twenty-fi-15b31d.mp3",
    "dur": 4.68
  },
  "Look at its shape: a slash, as in divide, and two small zeros, as in one hundred.": {
    "file": "look-at-its-shape-a-slash-as-in-divide-a-cecf45.mp3",
    "dur": 5.06
  },
  "Fifty percent is a half, and that is zero point five. Three ways to write the same amount.": {
    "file": "fifty-percent-is-a-half-and-that-is-zero-4cf0f5.mp3",
    "dur": 6.31
  },
  "One hundred percent is all of it: one whole.": {
    "file": "one-hundred-percent-is-all-of-it-one-who-0deae6.mp3",
    "dur": 2.76
  },
  "You will see percent on a battery: seventy-five percent full. As a decimal, that is zero point seven five.": {
    "file": "you-will-see-percent-on-a-battery-sevent-7b981e.mp3",
    "dur": 6.77
  },
  "And the point is used whenever we measure. Between two and three there are ten steps. This is two point three.": {
    "file": "and-the-point-is-used-whenever-we-measur-61f62b.mp3",
    "dur": 8.64
  },
  "Fill thirty percent of the square. Put on tens.": {
    "file": "fill-thirty-percent-of-the-square-put-on-6b6f06.mp3",
    "dur": 3.05
  },
  "Ten percent equals zero point one.": {
    "file": "ten-percent-equals-zero-point-one-5539ef.mp3",
    "dur": 2.11
  },
  "Nine point nine is not ten. But it is very close.": {
    "file": "nine-point-nine-is-not-ten-but-it-is-ver-baf7c6.mp3",
    "dur": 3.96
  },
  "How do we write \"nearly equal\"?": {
    "file": "how-do-we-write-nearly-equal-b9a9ab.mp3",
    "dur": 1.7
  },
  "Nine point nine on this side. Ten on that side. Will the beam stay level?": {
    "file": "nine-point-nine-on-this-side-ten-on-that-4ca726.mp3",
    "dur": 5.47
  },
  "Not quite. That side is a tiny bit heavier.": {
    "file": "not-quite-that-side-is-a-tiny-bit-heavie-30d8fd.mp3",
    "dur": 2.69
  },
  "Nine point nine is not equal to ten. True. But that does not say how close they are.": {
    "file": "nine-point-nine-is-not-equal-to-ten-true-ba1171.mp3",
    "dur": 5.16
  },
  "We need a sign for nearly equal.": {
    "file": "we-need-a-sign-for-nearly-equal-49c30f.mp3",
    "dur": 2.04
  },
  "This sign means approximately equal.": {
    "file": "this-sign-means-approximately-equal-908fa0.mp3",
    "dur": 2.09
  },
  "Nine point nine is approximately equal to ten.": {
    "file": "nine-point-nine-is-approximately-equal-t-c32b34.mp3",
    "dur": 2.57
  },
  "It is the equals sign, drawn with wavy lines. Nearly the same, but not exactly.": {
    "file": "it-is-the-equals-sign-drawn-with-wavy-li-462149.mp3",
    "dur": 5.83
  },
  "Add the missing tenth, and now it is exact. Only then do we write equals.": {
    "file": "add-the-missing-tenth-and-now-it-is-exac-6849dc.mp3",
    "dur": 5.33
  },
  "Rounding uses this sign. Ninety-eight is approximately one hundred, and one hundred is easier to work with.": {
    "file": "rounding-uses-this-sign-ninety-eight-is--e7f71e.mp3",
    "dur": 7.03
  },
  "Estimating uses it as well. Nineteen times five is hard to do in your head.": {
    "file": "estimating-uses-it-as-well-nineteen-time-bd66b7.mp3",
    "dur": 4.9
  },
  "But twenty times five is easy: one hundred.": {
    "file": "but-twenty-times-five-is-easy-one-hundre-f23bea.mp3",
    "dur": 2.42
  },
  "So nineteen times five is approximately one hundred.": {
    "file": "so-nineteen-times-five-is-approximately--5d2482.mp3",
    "dur": 3.34
  },
  "One divided by three is zero point three three three, and the threes never end. So we stop somewhere, and write approximately.": {
    "file": "one-divided-by-three-is-zero-point-three-3a085f.mp3",
    "dur": 8.26
  },
  "And measuring is always approximate. This rod is about seven and a half long.": {
    "file": "and-measuring-is-always-approximate-this-67559e.mp3",
    "dur": 5.35
  },
  "Twenty-eight is approximately how many? Put on tens.": {
    "file": "twenty-eight-is-approximately-how-many-p-ae2f7d.mp3",
    "dur": 3.24
  },
  "The square root of ten is approximately three point one six.": {
    "file": "the-square-root-of-ten-is-approximately--9cd4a0.mp3",
    "dur": 3.29
  },
  "Seven is three away from ten. So is thirteen.": {
    "file": "seven-is-three-away-from-ten-so-is-thirt-70603b.mp3",
    "dur": 3.05
  },
  "How do we write how far apart two numbers are?": {
    "file": "how-do-we-write-how-far-apart-two-number-9273ea.mp3",
    "dur": 2.28
  },
  "Here is three. And here, on the other side of zero, is minus three. Which one is further from zero?": {
    "file": "here-is-three-and-here-on-the-other-side-ead5ce.mp3",
    "dur": 8.33
  },
  "Three steps this way. And three steps that way. Both the same.": {
    "file": "three-steps-this-way-and-three-steps-tha-fe99b9.mp3",
    "dur": 3.91
  },
  "Minus three is less than three. But it is just as far from zero.": {
    "file": "minus-three-is-less-than-three-but-it-is-10281f.mp3",
    "dur": 4.9
  },
  "We need a sign for how far from zero.": {
    "file": "we-need-a-sign-for-how-far-from-zero-4b378f.mp3",
    "dur": 2.52
  },
  "These two bars mean absolute value.": {
    "file": "these-two-bars-mean-absolute-value-d2f2f5.mp3",
    "dur": 2.35
  },
  "The absolute value of minus three equals three.": {
    "file": "the-absolute-value-of-minus-three-equals-0064c3.mp3",
    "dur": 3.22
  },
  "The bars ask one thing: how far from zero? It does not matter which way.": {
    "file": "the-bars-ask-one-thing-how-far-from-zero-0e8e69.mp3",
    "dur": 5.45
  },
  "The absolute value of three is three as well. A distance is never less than zero.": {
    "file": "the-absolute-value-of-three-is-three-as--7323ff.mp3",
    "dur": 5.33
  },
  "The bars come in a pair, as brackets do: one before, and one after.": {
    "file": "the-bars-come-in-a-pair-as-brackets-do-o-e9b571.mp3",
    "dur": 4.34
  },
  "How far apart are two and five? Take one from the other, inside the bars. Either way round, the answer is three.": {
    "file": "how-far-apart-are-two-and-five-take-one--eb44c3.mp3",
    "dur": 7.54
  },
  "Minus five is less than three. But its absolute value is greater: it is further from zero.": {
    "file": "minus-five-is-less-than-three-but-its-ab-16501a.mp3",
    "dur": 6.46
  },
  "Use it when only the size of a gap matters. A guess of eight, when the answer is ten, is off by two.": {
    "file": "use-it-when-only-the-size-of-a-gap-matte-555e2d.mp3",
    "dur": 7.61
  },
  "How far is minus four from zero? Count the steps.": {
    "file": "how-far-is-minus-four-from-zero-count-th-b8585a.mp3",
    "dur": 3.17
  },
  "The absolute value of three minus eight equals five.": {
    "file": "the-absolute-value-of-three-minus-eight--a1638d.mp3",
    "dur": 3.26
  },
  "Some number, plus two, equals five.": {
    "file": "some-number-plus-two-equals-five-ffcb2f.mp3",
    "dur": 2.4
  },
  "What shall we call a number we do not know yet?": {
    "file": "what-shall-we-call-a-number-we-do-not-kn-be8cb3.mp3",
    "dur": 2.69
  },
  "Write what you see.": {
    "file": "write-what-you-see-c8d289.mp3",
    "dur": 1.03
  },
  "Make it true.": {
    "file": "make-it-true-f434f3.mp3",
    "dur": 0.89
  },
  "A clean run!": {
    "file": "a-clean-run-d8d817.mp3",
    "dur": 1.01
  },
  "Again, for the star?": {
    "file": "again-for-the-star-599440.mp3",
